### 4. Component Requirements Checklist

#### ✅ Basic Requirements
- [ ] Use functional component with hooks only
- [ ] Add React.memo for performance
- [ ] Include PropTypes with proper validation
- [ ] Provide default props where appropriate
- [ ] Use absolute imports (`utils/`, `components/`)
- [ ] Keep component under 300 lines

#### ✅ MUI Integration
- [ ] Use MUI components as base
- [ ] Apply consistent styling with SX prop only
- [ ] Include proper theme integration
- [ ] Add hover and focus states with SX
- [ ] Ensure accessibility (ARIA labels, roles)
- [ ] Use MUI's responsive breakpoint system

#### ✅ Financial App Specific
- [ ] Use `formatCurrency` for monetary values
- [ ] Include proper error handling
- [ ] Add loading states where needed
- [ ] Consider mobile responsiveness
- [ ] Include proper data validation

#### ✅ Testing
- [ ] Create test file: `__tests__/ComponentName.test.jsx`
- [ ] Test rendering with different props
- [ ] Test user interactions (clicks, hovers)
- [ ] Test accessibility compliance
- [ ] Test edge cases and error states

### 5. Test Template
```javascript
// src/components/__tests__/FundCard.test.jsx
import React from 'react'
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react'
import userEvent from '@testing-library/user-event'
import FundCard from '../FundCard'

const mockFund = {
  id: '1',
  name: 'HDFC Equity Fund',
  nav: 150.25,
  category: 'Equity',
  riskLevel: 'High',
  returns: 12.5
}

describe('FundCard', () => {
  it('renders fund information correctly', () => {
    render(<FundCard fund={mockFund} />)
    
    expect(screen.getByText('HDFC Equity Fund')).toBeInTheDocument()
    expect(screen.getByText('₹150.25')).toBeInTheDocument()
    expect(screen.getByText('Equity')).toBeInTheDocument()
  })

  it('calls onSelect when clicked', async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup()
    const mockOnSelect = jest.fn()
    
    render(<FundCard fund={mockFund} onSelect={mockOnSelect} />)
    
    await user.click(screen.getByRole('button'))
    expect(mockOnSelect).toHaveBeenCalledWith('1')
  })

  it('shows selected state when isSelected is true', () => {
    render(<FundCard fund={mockFund} isSelected={true} />)
    
    const card = screen.getByRole('button')
    expect(card).toHaveStyle('border: 2px solid #1976d2')
  })
})
```

### 6. Common Component Types

#### Form Components
- `AppTextField` - Enhanced MUI TextField
- `AppSelect` - Enhanced MUI Select
- `AppCheckbox` - Enhanced MUI Checkbox
- `AppRadioGroup` - Enhanced MUI RadioGroup

#### Display Components
- `CurrencyDisplay` - Formatted currency display
- `PercentageDisplay` - Formatted percentage display
- `DateDisplay` - Formatted date display
- `LoadingSpinner` - Consistent loading indicator

#### Layout Components
- `AppCard` - Standardized card component
- `AppModal` - Standardized modal component
- `AppDialog` - Standardized dialog component
- `AppTooltip` - Standardized tooltip component

#### Financial Components
- `FundCard` - Mutual fund display card
- `PortfolioSummary` - Portfolio overview
- `SIPCalculator` - SIP calculation widget
- `PerformanceChart` - Investment performance chart

### 7. Export Pattern
```javascript
// src/components/common/index.js
export { default as AppButton } from './AppButton.component'
export { default as AppTextField } from './AppTextField.component'
export { default as AppCard } from './AppCard.component'
export { default as AppModal } from './AppModal.component'

// Usage
import { AppButton, AppTextField } from 'components/common'
```